  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\u222c}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}-15{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[5{x}^{3}-3{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
